1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,450
A single subatomic particle just struck Earth traveling near light speed.

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:08,360
It packed the kinetic punch of a ninety-mile-an-hour fastball.

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:13,090
In 1991, Utah detectors registered a signal that shocked astrophysicists.

4
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:16,980
Protons are microscopic, yet this one carried forty million tera-electron-volts.

5
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:20,120
Pause. Can you guess what cosmic monster fired this ray?

6
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:25,400
Scientists named it the Oh-My-God particle, and nothing should create it.

7
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,770
Tracing its origin backward leads to empty space with no stars.

8
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:34,460
Current physics says this particle simply cannot exist in our universe.

9
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:39,150
Yet right now, another impossible traveler is racing toward us because...
